```

## Do not do these without explicit subgroup authorization and gates

- broad backend rewrite
- broad frontend rewrite
- destructive class/table/route/API renames
- production schema/data migration execution
- prompt replacement without analysis validation gates
- report renderer rewrite without ReportScope and validation gates
- corpus expansion without privacy/retention/scope/staleness gates
- export expansion without export-readiness/privacy gates
- GitHub Actions restoration
- cloud infrastructure automation changes
- enterprise org/workspace/RBAC/SSO/compliance/billing
- always-on enterprise availability

## Analysis boundary

The app may use therapeutic, psychological, behavioral, cognitive, relational, and diagnostic-framework-informed concepts as evidence-limited reasoning references.

It must not diagnose, confirm diagnosis, label a person as having a disorder, provide treatment authority, adjudicate misconduct, prove hidden intent, or pressure reconciliation in high-risk contexts.

## Sensitive content rule

Do not add logs, telemetry, lifecycle events, error text, debug output, or status messages containing transcript bodies, audio, prompts, raw completions, report bodies, exports, secrets, session tokens, or login codes.

## Compatibility posture

Prefer aliases, adapters, compatibility layers, and additive contracts before physical renames or destructive changes.

